<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gross Friedrichsburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1683</span> · Also known as Groß Friedrichsburg, Fort Hollandia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gross Friedrichsburg was a fort founded in 1683 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princes-town-ghana">Pokesu</a>, now Princes Town, on the western coast of Ghana. The chief post of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-african-company">Brandenburg African Company</a>, it was sold to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a> in 1717, though the local leader John Konny held it until 1724. Renamed Fort <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayapura">Hollandia</a>, it survives as a ruin and is part of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> World Heritage site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gross-friedrichsburg.jpg" alt="Gross Friedrichsburg" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fornax · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kriegsflagge_Kur-Brandenburgische_Flotte.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
